docs {
  # Matrix Parameter Backward Compatibility Tests
  
  End-to-end tests for SIF 3.3 matrix parameter backward compatibility.
  Tests inbound parsing (gateway), conflict detection, default injection,
  and the legacy tag toggle for outbound formatting.
  
  ## What This Tests
  
  1. Matrix params in URL are parsed and forwarded as headers
  2. Headers-only requests work (modern SIF 3.7 clients)
  3. Conflict between matrix params and headers returns 400
  4. Default zone injection when no zone specified
  5. Default context injection (always "DEFAULT")
  6. Entity tag SIF_LEGACY_MATRIX_PARAMS toggle
  
  ## Self-Contained
  
  This folder creates its own domain, solution, zone, and environments.
  The final test deletes the domain (cascade cleanup).
  
  ## Run Order
  
  Tests are numbered and must be run in sequence.
}
